WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.190
RAJAT KHANNA: As one of the
largest home improvement

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.100
retailers, our strategy
really revolves

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.700
around winning the customer and
better competing for the pro

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.630
by enabling both customer
segments to make homes better

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.450
for all from inspiration
to installation.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.050
We want our customers to have
the best experience with us,

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.860
regardless of how, when, or
where they choose to shop.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.800
For our dev ops,
look, our philosophy

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.800
is really an approach
to software development

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.850
that enables teams to build,
test, and release software

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.695
faster and more reliably.

00:00:39.695 --> 00:00:42.350
VIVEK BALIVADA: Did we
uncover anything surprising?

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.430
Yes.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.250
So our 300x increase
in release velocity

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.690
and GCP ability to support the
scaling was an added value.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:55.520
The power and potential of GCP
and our Google SI principles

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.310
enabled us to achieve a
lot of this automation very

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.490
seamlessly.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.240
And we were able to focus on
reliability and technology.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.780
An example of this includes
collaborating and strategizing,

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.170
the change request automation
process with IP service

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.165
management and optimizing our
regression and performance test

00:01:12.165 --> 00:01:12.665
suites.

00:01:12.665 --> 00:01:15.800
RAJAT KHANNA: And at the core
of our dev ops ecosystem,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.110
we have four
principles we follow,

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.922
ownership and accountability.

00:01:19.922 --> 00:01:21.380
What that really
means is our teams

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.750
are fully committed
from birth of an idea

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.280
to the product's launch.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.810
Systems thinking, performance of
the entire technology ecosystem

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:32.150
takes precedence
over the performance

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.070
of a specific theme.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.078
Continuous experimentation
and learning and automation.

00:01:37.078 --> 00:01:38.870
VIVEK BALIVADA: It's
an awesome experience,

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.137
you know, all the partnership,
the weekly calls that we

00:01:42.137 --> 00:01:43.220
have with the Google team.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.230
RAJAT KHANNA: So with our
dev ops transformation

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:49.850
to Google Cloud, we've gone
from doing 30 releases to more

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.850
than 4,500 releases per year.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.310
Look, what this means is
going from one release

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.890
every two weeks to
more than 20 releases

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.720
daily, a massive improvement.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.090
VIVEK BALIVADA: I'm so
excited to win this award.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.240
And it showcases our
team's journey, right,

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.760
how we continue to power our
dev ops and SI principles.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.090
RAJAT KHANNA: This award is
a recognition for both Google

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:11.960
and Lowe's.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.410
[MUSIC PLAYING]

